   2 \, \text{yogurts/day} \times 30 \, \text{days} = 60 \, \text{yogurts}
   $$

3. **Sale Offer**: 4 yogurts for $5.00. The cost per yogurt is not needed explicitly; we use the bundle to calculate how many sets are required.

4. **Number of Sets Needed**:  
   $$
   \frac{60}{4} = 15 \, \text{sets}
   $$

5. **Total Cost**:  
   $$
   15 \, \text{sets} \times \$5.00/\text{set} = \$75.00
   $$

