Then, a boy got 6 liters. So I need to add that to the 8 liters taken by the girls. 8 + 6 equals 14 liters. So altogether, they've taken 14 liters out of the original 24.

To find out how much is left, I subtract the total taken from the original amount. So 24 liters minus 14 liters. Let me check that: 24 minus 14 is 10. Wait, that seems straightforward, but let me verify each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.

